# Tool Input Validation

| Field | Value |
| ----- | ----- |
| Issue | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
| Status | Draft |

This specification defines the registry boundary for model-supplied tool input and preserves the existing tool-result path back to the model.

## Contract

- "'`ToolRegistry.execute` rejects missing required fields, wrong declared types and enum violations before executing a tool, returning a `ToolResponse` whose result names the property path and failed constraint; returned diagnostics and logs never include rejected input values, valid input including unknown keys passes through unchanged exactly once without coercion or defaults, and unknown tool names still throw `Unknown tool: <name>`.
- Static schemas compile at registration, invalid schemas throw an error naming the tool at registration, and ten subsequent executions reuse the compiled schema without reading it again.
- Function-valued definitions resolve the current schema on each execution, enforce that schema rather than a stale one, and cache compilation by resolved schema object identity.

## Integration and delivery

Rejections are ordinary tool results, allowing the existing orchestrator to return their text to the model for a corrected call within the five-tool-round default bound. The execute method'"'s one-line documentation points here for the rejection and unknown-name contract.

Delivery includes the validator as a runtime dependency, a MINOR version bump and consumer migration notes in the PR and changelog. README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md explain validation, unchanged extra properties and returned rejections; executors no longer receive malformed input for their own error handling. CI owns build/import, typechecking, lint and the full test suite.
EOF
